option.value:
# Styling Architecture

## Design Tokens

All design values live in CSS custom properties in `src/styles/globals.css`. This approach gives you:
- ✅ Zero runtime overhead (CSS native)
- ✅ Easy theme toggling (`:root` vs `@media (prefers-color-scheme: light)`)
- ✅ Portable tokens (work across any framework)
- ✅ Debuggable in browser DevTools

### Color System

```css
/* Background layers (depth) */
--bg-base:        #0A0A0A;   /* page background */
--bg-surface:     #111111;   /* cards, panels */
--bg-elevated:    #1A1A1A;   /* hover states, code */
--bg-overlay:     #222222;   /* tooltips */

/* Text hierarchy */
--text-primary:   #EDEDEC;   /* headings, labels */
--text-secondary: #888884;   /* body copy */
--text-tertiary:  #555552;   /* disabled, hint text */

/* Accent (single, used sparingly) */
--accent:         #0052CC;   /* links, CTAs */
--accent-hover:   #0747A6;
--accent-subtle:  #0A1929;   /* badge backgrounds */
```

### Spacing Grid

8pt base unit for all spacing:
```css
--space-1:  4px;
--space-2:  8px;
--space-3:  12px;
--space-4:  16px;
--space-5:  20px;
--space-6:  24px;
--space-8:  32px;
--space-10: 40px;
--space-12: 48px;
--space-16: 64px;
--space-20: 80px;
```

### Typography

```css
--font-sans: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
--font-mono: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', 'Courier New', monospace;

/* Base sizes */
h1: 40px, weight 400, tracking -0.025em
h2: 32px, weight 400, tracking -0.02em
h3: 24px, weight 500
body: 15px, line 1.65
ui-label: 13px, monospace, uppercase
```

### Borders & Radius

```css
/* Deliberately tight = technical feel */
--radius-sm:  4px;   /* chips, badges */
--radius-md:  6px;   /* buttons */
--radius-lg:  8px;   /* cards */
--radius-xl:  12px;  /* modals */

/* Border opacity */
--border-subtle:  rgba(255,255,255,0.06);   /* light dividers */
--border-default: rgba(255,255,255,0.10);   /* hover borders */
--border-strong:  rgba(255,255,255,0.18);   /* focus rings */
```

## Component Styles

All component styles are defined in `globals.css`. No CSS-in-JS or external stylesheets.

### Chip Component

```css
.chip {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  border: 0.5px solid var(--border-default);
  color: var(--text-secondary);
  padding: 3px 8px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  display: inline-block;
}

.chip-accent {
  background: var(--accent-subtle);
  border-color: var(--accent);
  color: var(--accent);
}
```

### Button Component

```css
.btn-primary {
  background: var(--text-primary);
  color: var(--text-inverse);
  font-size: 13px;
  padding: 10px 20px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  border: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background var(--transition-fast);
}
.btn-primary:hover {
  background: var(--accent);
}

.btn-secondary {
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--text-primary);
  border: 0.5px solid var(--border-default);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: 10px 20px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all var(--transition-base);
}
.btn-secondary:hover {
  border-color: var(--border-strong);
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
}
```

### Project Card

```css
.project-card {
  background: var(--bg-surface);
  border: 0.5px solid var(--border-subtle);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: 28px;
  transition: background var(--transition-base),
              border-color var(--transition-base);
}
.project-card:hover {
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  border-color: var(--border-default);
}
```

### Nav Link with Underline Draw

```css
.nav-link {
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--text-secondary);
  position: relative;
  transition: color var(--transition-base);
}

.nav-link::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  bottom: -2px;
  left: 0;
  width: 0;
  height: 1px;
  background: var(--accent);
  transition: width var(--transition-base) ease;
}

.nav-link:hover,
.nav-link.active {
  color: var(--text-primary);
}

.nav-link:hover::after,
.nav-link.active::after {
  width: 100%;
}
```

### Metric Card

```css
.metric-val {
  font-size: 28px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  color: var(--text-primary);
}

.metric-label {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  color: var(--text-tertiary);
  margin-top: 4px;
}
```

### Section Label

```css
.section-label {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--text-tertiary);
  margin-bottom: 32px;
}
```

## Layout Utilities

All layouts use inline `style` objects in React components for maximum flexibility:

```tsx
// Container with max-width
<div
  style={{
    maxWidth: 'var(--content-width)',  // 720px
    marginLeft: 'auto',
    marginRight: 'auto',
    paddingLeft: 'var(--page-padding)',  // 40px
    paddingRight: 'var(--page-padding)',
  }}
>
  {children}
</div>

// Grid layout
<div
  style={{
    display: 'grid',
    gridTemplateColumns: 'repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr))',
    gap: 'var(--space-6)',
  }}
>
  {items}
</div>

// Flex layout
<div
  style={{
    display: 'flex',
    gap: 'var(--space-4)',
    flexWrap: 'wrap',
  }}
>
  {items}
</div>
```

## Transitions

```css
--transition-fast:   100ms ease;      /* hover states */
--transition-base:   200ms ease;      /* normal interactions */
--transition-slow:   350ms ease;      /* modal appearances */
```

## Responsive Design

Currently no breakpoints defined. The design is:
- ✅ Mobile-first (no overflow)
- ✅ Readable at any size (content width capped at 720px)
- ✅ Vertical rhythm maintained (8pt grid)

If you need responsive behavior, add this to `globals.css`:

```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  :root {
    --page-padding: 20px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 32px;
  }
}
```

## Dark Mode

The entire theme is dark mode first. If you want to add a light mode toggle:

```css
/* Light mode override */
html.light-mode {
  --bg-base:        #FAFAFA;
  --bg-surface:     #FFFFFF;
  --bg-elevated:    #F4F4F4;
  --text-primary:   #111111;
  --text-secondary: #666666;
  /* ... etc ... */
}
```

Then in your layout:

```tsx
const toggleDarkMode = () => {
  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('light-mode');
};
```

## Adding New Components

When creating a new component:

1. **Define styles in `globals.css`**
   ```css
   .my-component {
     background: var(--bg-surface);
     /* use design tokens only */
   }
   ```

2. **Reference in component**
   ```tsx
   export function MyComponent() {
     return <div className="my-component">...</div>
   }
   ```

3. **Never use inline styles for repeated patterns**
   - Creates maintenance debt
   - Hard to update globally
   - Reduces component reusability

## Testing the Theme

Open browser DevTools and toggle CSS variables:

```javascript
// Try dark theme
document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--accent', '#FF5500');

// See theme in real-time
```

---

**Key Principle:** All styling flows through CSS custom properties. This makes the theme completely portable and auditable.

import type { Metadata } from 'next'
import { Navbar } from '@/components/Navbar'
import { Footer } from '@/components/Footer'
import '@/styles/globals.css'

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Rohil Varma — Senior Software Engineer',
  description:
    'Turning ambiguous requirements into maintainable, observable systems at scale. Backend systems, distributed architecture, platform engineering.',
  openGraph: {
    title: 'Rohil Varma — Senior Software Engineer',
    description: 'Backend systems, distributed architecture, platform engineering.',
    type: 'website',
  },
}

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <head>
        <meta charSet="utf-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
      </head>
      <body>
        <Navbar />
        <main
          style={{
            maxWidth: 'var(--content-width)',
            marginLeft: 'auto',
            marginRight: 'auto',
            paddingLeft: 'var(--page-padding)',
            paddingRight: 'var(--page-padding)',
          }}
        >
          {children}
        </main>
        <Footer />
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}

import { Hero } from '@/components/Hero'
import { ProjectGrid } from '@/components/projects/ProjectGrid'
import { getProjects } from '@/lib/projects'

export default async function Home() {
  const projects = await getProjects()

  return (
    <>
      <Hero />
      <div id="work" style={{ paddingTop: 'var(--space-20)', paddingBottom: 'var(--space-20)' }}>
        <ProjectGrid projects={projects} />
      </div>
    </>
  )
}

import { MDXRemote } from 'next-mdx-remote/rsc'
import { notFound } from 'next/navigation'
import { getProjectBySlug, getProjects } from '@/lib/projects'
import { Chip } from '@/components/ui/Chip'
import { MetricCard } from '@/components/ui/MetricCard'
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/Button'

interface ProjectPageProps {
  params: {
    slug: string
  }
}

export async function generateStaticParams() {
  const projects = await getProjects()
  return projects.map((project) => ({
    slug: project.slug,
  }))
}

export default async function ProjectPage({ params }: ProjectPageProps) {
  const project = await getProjectBySlug(params.slug)

  if (!project) {
    notFound()
  }

  return (
    <article style={{ paddingTop: 'var(--space-20)', paddingBottom: 'var(--space-20)' }}>
      <div style={{ marginBottom: 'var(--space-10)' }}>
        <h1 style={{ marginBottom: 'var(--space-3)' }}>{project.title}</h1>
        <p
          style={{
            fontSize: '15px',
            color: 'var(--text-secondary)',
            marginBottom: 'var(--space-6)',
          }}
        >
          {project.tagline}
        </p>

        <div
          style={{
            display: 'flex',
            gap: 'var(--space-4)',
            flexWrap: 'wrap',
            marginBottom: 'var(--space-8)',
          }}
        >
          {project.stack.map((tech) => (
            <Chip key={tech} label={tech} />
          ))}
        </div>

        <div style={{ display: 'flex', gap: 'var(--space-8)', marginBottom: 'var(--space-8)' }}>
          <div>
            <div className="metric-label">Role</div>
            <div className="metric-val" style={{ fontSize: '16px' }}>
              {project.role}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div className="metric-label">Year</div>
            <div className="metric-val" style={{ fontSize: '16px' }}>
              {project.year}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div className="metric-label">Team Size</div>
            <div className="metric-val" style={{ fontSize: '16px' }}>
              {project.teamSize}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div
          style={{
            borderTop: '0.5px solid var(--border-subtle)',
            paddingTop: 'var(--space-6)',
            marginBottom: 'var(--space-10)',
          }}
        >
          <p style={{ marginBottom: 'var(--space-4)', color: 'var(--text-tertiary)' }}>
            Key outcomes
          </p>
          <div style={{ display: 'flex', flexWrap: 'wrap' }}>
            {project.outcomes.map((outcome) => (
              <MetricCard key={outcome.label} metric={outcome} />
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        style={{
          fontSize: '15px',
          lineHeight: 1.8,
          color: 'var(--text-secondary)',
        }}
        className="prose"
      >
        <MDXRemote source={project.content} />
      </div>

      <div
        style={{
          borderTop: '0.5px solid var(--border-subtle)',
          paddingTop: 'var(--space-10)',
          marginTop: 'var(--space-20)',
        }}
      >
        <Button href="/" variant="secondary">
          ← Back to Work
        </Button>
      </div>
    </article>
  )
}
